%% showcase: zenuml ref fragments
%% prose: `ref(Name)` draws a reference to another interaction — UML's interaction use — as a `ref` frame of its own row with the name centred. `ref(Name, A, B)` spans the named participants' heads, leftmost to rightmost; with none named it spans every participant. A quoted argument is the name wherever it stands, so `ref(A, B, "Name")` reads the same.
%% approx: The frame is as wide as the named participants' heads; ZenUML sizes it to its own fragment layout.
zenuml
    @Actor Shopper
    Shopper->Shop.checkout(cart) {
      ref(Authenticate, Shopper, Shop)
      Shop->Payments.charge(total) {
        ref("Fraud screening", Payments)
      }
      ref(Fulfilment)
    }
